  "inter_block_fanout": {
    "router": "route_fanout (generate.py): a reserved-track channel router over the escape pins -- one horizontal Metal3 trunk per net in the channel below the slices, one vertical Metal2 lane per net and side (west of the address latch, and in the wordline fan-out gap below the array), one Metal3 track per net in the decoder approach band. A lane and a trunk cross on different layers; the only vias are where a net turns",
    "escape_router": "MazeRouter: route_slice_escape brings the nine bit_slice ports to reserved Metal2 pins on the slice's bottom edge (drawn once for all 32 slices); route_hier brings the BLOCK_ESCAPES ports of addr_latch, control, row_decoder, data_latch and out_latch to a pin the maze picks on one block edge (connect_edge), on the layer the macro level carries on in, so the two wires merge with no via on the boundary",
